{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290499-technocratic-spheres-learning-restrictions","id":1290499,"title":"Technocratic Spheres learning restrictions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-21T12:58:51-08:00","id":1290499,"title":"Technocratic Spheres learning restrictions","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I would like to know for M20, what are the restrictions on the Technocratic Alternative Spheres? As I understand them: <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Data (Correspondence): Any infotech based paradigm can learn this, Virtual Adepts, NWO, and every technocracy member that wants to.</li> <li>Dimensional Science (Spirit): Only Void Engineers.</li> <li>Primal Utilities (Prime): Only Syndicate members. (Can other Technocrats also learn it? Can any economic related paradigms?)</li> </ol><br /> If a Void Engineer can learn Primal Utilities and Data, would it make sense for them to do so? A paragon of the 3 unique Technocratic Spheres has a place in the Void Engineers? If so, what is that place?<br /> <br /> Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-21-2019, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T13:15:53-08:00","id":1290508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290499-technocratic-spheres-learning-restrictions#post1290499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[*]Dimensional Science (Spirit): Only Void Engineers.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Officially'. but it seems that other groups can actually learn it these days - or rather, get it taught by the Void Engineeers - if rarely. The Iteration X splat writeup mentions<br /> &quot;This group has no use<br /> for \u201cfuzzy\u201d paradigms, so the Sphere of Dimensional<br /> Science is an extremely rare discipline among its ranks.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it seems Iteration X, at least, get basics taught by Void Engineers - which makes sense, given that they provide some of the gadgets for the VE's. But I presume even the ItXers that have it almost never have it at high levels unless they, ahem, continue personal studies outside of official protocol.<br /> <br /> I presume the same goes for Primal Utility in the way that it's is a very Syndicate exclusive sphere, because it directly ties to the paradigm they came up with. They could in theory teach it to others, and all it takes is to take the Merit that allows you to be trained by two Traiditions/Conventions to take it with good justification..but given the whole nature of the sphere, it *needs* to be part of your paradigm. And it's a weeeird paradigm. One of the most exotic there is, IMO.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T13:17:09-08:00","id":1290509,"title":"","content":"I feel like these spheres should available to anyone for whom they'd make sense but the trick becomes how did they learn? Each sphere is a particular body of knowledge within a particular paradigm. I could see a Chaotician viewing prime in a somewhat similar way to a Syndicate member, but he Syndicate member has the benefit of an unbroken chain of knowledge from the High Guild to the Invisible Exchequer to the modern Syndicate where as the Chaotician may see prime closer to their Traditional brethren but be able to take advantage of wellsprings and conjunctions more easily than someone else. Nodes become &quot;nodal points&quot;, points where intersecting waves of probabilistic contingencies converge allowing for excess variance that can be then applied to other causes to change an expected outcome distribution. So unless that Chaotician were a Syndicate renegade, they'd learn prime but with their own twist.<br /> <br /> As for Dim Sci, that strikes me as something common across all Technocrats and _maybe_ extending to exceptionally scientific other paradigms, even more so rigidly hewing to contemporary science than the SoE.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-21T13:32:47-08:00","id":1290513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290499-technocratic-spheres-learning-restrictions#post1290499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Greetings,<br /> <br /> I would like to know for M20, what are the restrictions on the Technocratic Alternative Spheres? As I understand them:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Data (Correspondence): Any infotech based paradigm can learn this, Virtual Adepts, NWO, and every technocracy member that wants to.</li> <li>Dimensional Science (Spirit): Only Void Engineers.</li> <li>Primal Utilities (Prime): Only Syndicate members. (Can other Technocrats also learn it? Can any economic related paradigms?)</li> </ol>If a Void Engineer can learn Primal Utilities and Data, would it make sense for them to do so? A paragon of the 3 unique Technocratic Spheres has a place in the Void Engineers? If so, what is that place?<br /> <br /> Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>Not canon, but I'm very keen on hypereconomics being a feature of the VAs. It's just that a VA is more likely to be robbing a bank to gain Primal Energy than building up a business. Dealing with cryptocurrency, digital economy.<br /> <br /> So Primal Utility for VAs at my table, BUT only if their practice is Hypereconomics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:23:19-08:00","id":1290685,"title":"","content":"Expanding on that, it isn\u2019t membership in the Syndicate that gets you access to Primal Utility; it\u2019s having the Practice of Hypereconomics. Similarly, I\u2019m pretty sure that there are Paradigms and/or Practices that serve as gateways to Data and Dimensional Science as well. You\u2019ll find those Paradigms and Practices among the ones incorporated into the NWO Focus and VE Focus, respectively, which is why the NWO and VEs can employ these Sphere variants; but <i>anyone</i> with the right Focus can access them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:52:47-08:00","id":1290695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290499-technocratic-spheres-learning-restrictions?p=1290685#post1290685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Expanding on that, it isn\u2019t membership in the Syndicate that gets you access to Primal Utility; it\u2019s having the Practice of Hypereconomics. Similarly, I\u2019m pretty sure that there are Paradigms and/or Practices that serve as gateways to Data and Dimensional Science as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, can you help me with a page number?<br /> <br /> In the M20 Dimensional Science write up, it is clearly stated that <i>only</i> Void Engineers are taught it. And the Data intro explicitly states that NWO and Virtual Adepts learn it, and share it with allies.<br /> <br /> Nothing so specific about Primal Utility, so is it Technocracy only? Syndicate only? Hypereconomics only?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 02-22-2019, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T03:27:57-08:00","id":1290707,"title":"","content":"Data is also a realm of the Virtual Adepts, so they are the prime example of that sphere being used outside the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Primal utility is, yes, hypereconomics only.<br /> Now, Hypereconomics pretty much got invented by the Syndicate, who then spread the concept of modern economy across the world. The concept of enlightened Hypereconomics still could have made it outside of the Technocratic Union though through two means:<br /> * Syndicate deserters, of course<br /> * A mortal heavily invested and studied in modern economy suddenly having their Awakening *through* that involvement. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> That'd be a case of a Mage with a very probable hypereconomic paradigm, without any involvement in the Syndicate whatsover. If the Syndics don't manage to get to them first.<br /> <br /> Along the same lines, other Orphans that awakened along certain worldviews (Fringe Science, Technomancy) could in theory gain Data or Dimensional Science - they'd simply need to reach the same conclusions as the respective Convention regarding those spheres.<br /> <br /> The spheres are a result of paradigm, after all - not an origin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 02-22-2019, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T09:55:29-08:00","id":1290808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290499-technocratic-spheres-learning-restrictions?p=1290513#post1290513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (...) It's just that a VA is more likely to be robbing a bank to gain Primal Energy than building up a business. (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think so ? Is this because Virtual Adepts have a history of actions against the Technocracy ? Or maybe because you see the Virtual Adepts as not established well in regard to institutions of mundane humans, and related businesses ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T12:05:53-08:00","id":1290866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1290499-technocratic-spheres-learning-restrictions?p=1290808#post1290808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think so ? Is this because Virtual Adepts have a history of actions against the Technocracy ? Or maybe because you see the Virtual Adepts as not established well in regard to institutions of mundane humans, and related businesses ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm thinking of anarchist &quot;anonymous&quot; type VAs, deciding to simply pull a heist and run off with a huge amount of Syndicate assets. Basically framing VA Primal Utility as being about digital economy, crowdfunding, illegal activity which is framed as moral, cryptocurrencies... as opposed to the traditional venture capital of the Technocracy. There's going to be overlap of course. Syndicate types who deal with crypto or with charities, or who perform &quot;rogue transactions&quot; against assets outside of the syndicate's reach (read, robberies). VAs who take part in traditional finance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 02-22-2019, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}